  "_form": "Pradhan Mantri Ujjwala Yojana — UJJWALA KYC Application, Version 5.0",
  "_source": "https://www.pmuy.gov.in/documents/KYC.pdf (Referer: ujjwala2.html), 458536 bytes",
  "_notes": [
    "Row indices are extract-form-boxes.py's own ordering, the same one",
    "scripts/row-detail.py prints. Cell counts are pinned so a re-issued",
    "form fails the build rather than shifting a citizen's Aadhaar one column.",
    "",
    "The form's habit throughout: a tick is the NARROW cell that follows the",
    "cell holding its printed word. Confirmed on the migrant row by eye, then",
    "found again on caste, both Yes/No declarations, cylinder and burner.",
    "",
    "POA code: the footnote lists the codes as POA01..POA25, so the form",
    "pre-prints P, O and A in three boxes and leaves two for the digits.",
    "",
    "Page 2 is not mapped. Its header reads 'To be filled by Dealer/Distributor",
    "based on the category in which applicant is applying' — the category table,",
    "the LPG ID and the acknowledgement slip all belong to the distributor, not",
    "the citizen. FormMitra should leave that page untouched and say so.",
    "",
    "NEEDS ABHISHEK'S EYE — two calls made from geometry alone:",
    "  contactMobile (R12): the row offers a 4-box run right after the printed",
    "  'Mobile No.:' and a 12-box run at the far right, split by the same 35.22pt",
    "  gutter column that carries the right-hand label on every address row.",
    "  A 10-digit number only fits the 12-box run, so that is what is mapped.",
    "  address.areaPostOffice2 (R16): 'Area / Post Office Name' is one label",
    "  merged down two rows, so the field is two lines of boxes. On the second",
    "  line the form forgot two verticals, leaving cell 26 three boxes wide.",
    "",
    "KNOWN FORM DEFECT: bank.ifsc has 10 boxes for an 11-character IFSC code.",
    "Not a mapping error — the row really is one box short. Whatever fills it",
    "has to say so rather than silently drop a character.",
    "",
    "LEFT UNNAMED ON PURPOSE: R10 cells 8-25, R19 and R20 cells 21-33. Combs",
    "with no printed label anywhere near them; this form leaves stray grid.",
    "",
    "DOB TRAP: row 8 is the printed 'D D M M Y Y Y Y' guide, not an entry row.",
    "The boxes the citizen writes in are row 10 cells 18-25, directly under it",
    "and at the same x span (424.9-538.3). Mapping dob to row 8 overstruck the",
    "guide letters and left the real boxes empty; caught by looking at the",
    "stamped output, not by any checker. Row 10 therefore carries two unrelated",
    "fields, which is why it is named casteDob."
  ],
